            <ArticleTitle>Giant adrenal myelolipoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1116-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adrenal myelolipomas are nonfunctioning benign tumors composed of hematopoietic elements and mature adipose tissue. These tumors usually remain small and asymptomatic; occasionally, however, they reach massive proportions and become symptomatic. To date, only two giant adrenal myelolipomas (&gt;4,000 g) have been described in the literature. We describe the diagnostic evaluation and the operative management of the third largest adrenal myelolipoma reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
